- # CMIC Skill Scanner
- Security scanner that analyzes skill source code before installation.
- **Source code**: https://gitee.com/random_player/cmic-skill-scanner
- | Version | `v0.6.4` |
- ## Source Code & Verification
- - **Repository**: https://gitee.com/random_player/cmic-skill-scanner
- - **Checksums**: https://gitee.com/random_player/cmic-skill-scanner/raw/main/releases/v0.6.4/SHA256SUMS
- - **Releases**: https://gitee.com/random_player/cmic-skill-scanner/releases/v0.6.4
- ## What This Scanner Does
- This tool reads skill source files you specify and reports findings. It analyzes the skill's code, not your system.
- ## Usage
- skillscan review /path/to/skill --format markdown
- skillscan review /path/to/skills --output-dir ./results
- ## What It Detects in Skills
- | Category | Suspicious Pattern |
- |----------|-------------------|
- | Network calls | curl/wget to unknown URLs, calls to IP addresses |
- | Obfuscation | base64 decode, eval/exec with external input, minified code |
- | Credential access | skill attempts to read ~/.ssh, ~/.aws, ~/.config |
- | Permission requests | skill requests elevated/sudo, modifies system files |
- | Data exfiltration | skill uploads to external servers, sends credentials |
- **Note**: These are patterns the scanner detects IN the skill being analyzed, not actions the scanner performs.
